<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cicones</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ciconians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cicones were a Thracian people living on the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> coast near Ismarus and Maroneia. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a> they are allies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odysseus">Odysseus</a> sacks their town of Ismarus, where the priest Maron gives him the strong wine later used against the Cyclops. Greek colonists settled in their territory from the 7th century BCE.</p></div>
